   "text": {
    "L1": "In dry places, rain may fall on only a few days each year.",
    "L2": "The main idea is not one interesting detail. It is how people collected and stored rainwater.",
    "L3": "Rainwater flowed down the gently sloping ground into an underground tank called a taanka.",
    "L4": "The tank stored water for the dry months, when little rain was available.",
    "L5": "A lid kept the stored water clean and cool.",
    "L6": "So the whole text is about collecting and conserving water, not just about the lid or the heat.",
    "L7": "At home, we should save water by closing the tap while brushing."
   },
